{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8qhDVfUiLZhh27t3z5s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found one problem: a play whose setup fails never releases its server hold. Otherwise the combined change matches the spec, and the unit suite passes (4471 of 4471). The finding is in `.nightralph/findings.md`, which is not staged or committed.\n\n**The finding (low severity).** In `src/renderer/controllers/playback-controller.js:260`, `openPlayer` asks the engine for a server before it checks that the file can be played. When that check fails with `UnplayableFileError`, `location-history` never runs the page's `destroy` hook, so `closePlayer` is skipped. The server hold is never released and the play's engine subscriptions stay armed. The next play then overwrites the recorded info hash, so the first hold leaks for good. This path is rare (a torrent with no playable file, or a stale \"most recent file\" on forward navigation), and the bug existed before this branch. But it still breaks the spec's rule that every hold is released when its play ends.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- **Engine server holds:** I compared the code against webtorrent 1.9.7's destroy order. The torrent is removed from the client before `close` fires, so the guard against duplicate adds in `torrentClose` holds. The default whole-torrent selection is added on `metadata`, so replacing it on the first selection call is right. The early start-then-stop test does tell the fixed code from the old code: before the fix it gets a server reply whose port accepts connections.\n- **Renderer:** the resume list, the error list, the dispatcher memo, the player page unmount, and the poster job timeout all look correct.\n- **Host:** the single-thread debounce, the reaping of the external player when `try_wait` errors, and the VLC probe timeout all look correct.\n\nTwo things I saw but did not list, because they are older than this branch and outside the spec:\n1. A `wt-select-files` that arrives while the torrent is still verifying gets undone when `ready` re-applies the selections it started with.\n2. If a torrent is stopped and resumed while the player still holds its server, closing the player can release a hold taken by someone else, such as a poster job.\n\nRunning the tests rebuilt `build/`, and I wrote the test log to `/tmp/wtd-review-unit.log`, which is outside the worktree."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1085,"cache_read_input_tokens":89126,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1085},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b348075c-63cf-4192-a3b5-b85f5599b80b","uuid":"3d390e83-c58e-4597-913a-f024508030a1","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:32:44.026Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8qhDCJXbmWVet8gs8oe"}
